SM(406,{"n":"Deuteronomy 18","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 18.mp3","d":2468.2,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[22.8,"We'll go ahead and uh get started."],[25.52,"When we get started, we're gonna be picking up in uh Deuteronomy chapter 18."],[32.24,"So, while it has not been a long time for the people listening to this recording in the future, all the way in the year 2000."],[42.48,"It's been a long time since we rocked and rolled uh here in uh Lafayette, Louisiana, because we're coming back post-Lent and Posca break."],[55.2,"So we do need to do a little bit of catch-up, but fortunately not too much catch-up because we're smack in the middle, literally in terms of chapters."],[66.52,"There are 34 chapters in the book of Deuteronomy, and we finished chapter 17."],[71.64,"So we are smack in the middle of the book of Deuteronomy, and we are smack in the middle of what most of the text of Deuteronomy is, which is Moses' final oration, his final sermon, his final homily."],[88.28,"Uh the people of Israel as he is preparing uh to pass away."],[93.08,"He is preparing to pass leadership on to Joshua, and the people on the plains of Moab are preparing to cross the Jordan River and go in to take possession of the land of Canaan."],[104.96,"And so, since we're in the middle of this final oration, final sermon, we picked a decent place to stop where he was changing topics."],[117.44,"And so that means we don't have to spend a huge amount of time running through."],[122.32,"But in brief, the last few things he talked about were concerned with the celebration of the feasts once they come into the land."],[135.8,"Means the second law, the second Torah, because the things he's talking to them about and reminding them about, whether it's events in the recent past, or whether it's commandments, or whether it's feasts and sacrifices, all of these things are things we've already read about in the previous books of the Torah."],[157.66,"Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers, that talked about those events, talked about those commandments, talked about those feasts, talked about all of those, the sacrifices, all of those things."],[167.58,"Moses is now highlighting certain things and talking about specific things."],[172.62,"And the things he's been talking about, immediately preceding where we start tonight, are all things that have to be kind of reapplied in terms of the land that they're coming into."],[185.26,"Because remember, now for 42 years, they've been living in the desert in a camp."],[193.66,"And this is the second generation."],[197.14,"The whole first generation that came out of Egypt has died."],[200.82,"Meaning this generation has spent pretty much their whole life, if not their whole life, living in this camp in the wilderness."],[210.84,"So this is the life that they've known with the tabernacle in the middle of the camp, the courtyard, and then the tribes camped around it."],[219.53,"And so the way they celebrate the Day of Atonement every year is based on living in this camp."],[227.15,"And having the tabernacle in the center."],[229.92,"Now they're gonna be coming and settling in the land of Canaan."],[233.6,"They're gonna be permanently settled on the land."],[236.0,"There's gonna be one place where the tabernacle and then the temple is going to be, but they're gonna be spread out over this big geographic, they're not gonna be all camped together in a circle."],[245.48,"They're gonna be spread out across the land."],[248.14,"So there's gonna be different things involved in terms of travel to get to the sanctuary and all these things."],[253.58,"And so the way the Day of Atonement is celebrated is gonna be a little bit different, at least for some of them."],[259.66,"The ones who are living right around the sanctuary may be not so different, but the ones who are far away, it'll be a little different."],[265.98,"Way Passover is celebrated, a little different."],[269.26,"Um, all these things that are changes, that are gonna happen once they come into the land."],[274.96,"And so Moses is sort of taking the previous commandments regarding the feasts and reapplying them to this new context of them being settled in the land."],[286.36,"He's going to do the same thing, a bunch of other things."],[289.64,"And most recently he talked about when they have a king."],[293.08,"Not going to go into that all over again."],[295.32,"We'll come back to it when we get into First Kingdoms or First Samuel and read every Puritan's favorite misinterpreted passage that they claim is anti king because they forget about this whole Deuteronomy thing where God tells them what kind of king to have."],[311.32,"But that in and of itself, the idea that they're going to have a quote unquote civil government, that's not something you have when you're living in a camp out in the desert."],[323.52,"But once you go and you settle in towns and cities, there are various government functions that are gonna have to happen in those towns and cities and villages over the tribes, over the nation as a whole."],[339.98,"Those things are gonna have to be organized."],[341.58,"There are gonna be people who are in charge of that."],[344.2,"And so commandments and structures and things that had to do with the leadership in the camp, like the elders of the tribes and the elders of the people, those have to be adapted to the new living situation."],[356.06,"And so that's what Moses is doing."],[357.98,"He's sort of, this is not just his final address in terms of like, you know, it's traditional for an American president to give to say something on their way out."],[370.08,"Probably Eisenhower's is the most famous one because he warned us about everything that has happened since the since the year 1960."],[379.2,"But that's right, this a farewell address."],[382.56,"It's not just a farewell address."],[384.56,"This is also the last time that Moses is kind of utilizing the authority that God gave him that we already saw."],[391.68,"The authority to take right what God had spoken to him and apply it to the lives of the people."],[398.8,"This is sort of his last time doing that."],[401.2,"That's why this is the last book of Moses."],[404.08,"This is the last of the Torah"],[406.25,"He's going to be handing that authority on to Joshua to do that going forward."],[412.57,"And so that's sort of what Moses is doing."],[416.01,"And as I said, he's kind of changing topics here as we get started tonight."],[420.65,"So unless there are any leftover comments, questions, uh, advertisements, or RSVPs for Pajopest 26."],[431.37,"Uh, we will go ahead and pick up in Deuteronomy chapter 18, verse 1."],[437.77,"The priests, the Levites, all the tribe of Levi, shall have no part nor inheritance with Israel."],[446.97,"The burnt offerings of the Lord shall be their portion."],[449.89,"These they shall eat."],[451.53,"Therefore, they shall have no inheritance among their brethren."],[454.41,"The Lord is their inheritance, as he said to them."],[458.09,"So again, this is being reiterated."],[460.71,"And what it means that they have no inheritance, doesn't mean they don't get to pass anything on to their children."],[466.09,"Inheritance here is talking about the land allotments."],[470.31,"We read about those in numbers."],[472.55,"That not just each tribe, but each clan, each family, got their allotted piece of land."],[481.17,"And the Levites do not get any land."],[484.45,"Now, pretty much all of Israel is doing, the vast majority of it is doing subsistence farming."],[490.53,"So you're given that land, you plant that land, you grow crops, you use that to feed your family."],[497.73,"So the Levites have families, the priests have families, all of them have families."],[502.81,"They don't have land."],[504.41,"So this raises the question of okay, how are they going to eat?"],[509.29,"How are they going to support themselves?"],[510.81,"How are they going to do these things?"],[512.42,"Because God has set this up."],[514.52,"Why has He not given them land?"],[516.28,"Not as a punishment for something."],[518.7,"But they're called to be priests."],[520.22,"They're called to serve God sort of full time."],[523.32,"They're called to operate the sanctuary and the things around it."],[526.52,"They're called to be there for the spiritual needs of the people."],[529.26,"To offer sacrifices."],[530.86,"That's sort of their full-time job."],[532.78,"And if they have to also operate a farm to feed their family, they're not going to be able to do that."],[538.55,"They can't do both."],[540.43,"Okay? And so God doesn't give them land to work."],[543.83,"And so now Moses is going to describe how the situation should be set up to account for that."],[550.75,"Now this shall be the judgment concerning the priests from the people, from those who offer sacrifices, whether it is a young bull or a sheep, one shall give to the priest the shoulder, the cheeks, and the stomach."],[564.03,"The first fruits of your grain, wine, and olive oil, and the first fruit of the sheep's fleece you shall give to him."],[570.59,"But the Lord your God chose him out of all your tribes to stand before the Lord your God, to minister and to bless in his name, he and his sons forever among the children of Israel."],[582.03,"So they receive the tithes, the offerings, portions of them that the rest of the tribes bring to offer to God."],[589.39,"Portion of those goes to the priests"],[594.1,"And there's a certain logic to this, which the people should not protest, because they're bringing all of this to God."],[605.78,"So if you give the animal, the grain, the wine, the oil, if you give it to God, God can then do whatever he wants with it."],[613.62,"And if so, if God wants to give part of that to the Levites, this should be this should be fine with you."],[622.74,"Okay This is something, and this may go to unpopular places, but I'm not worried about that."],[630.78,"But this is in our modern society, we have a very different relationship to money and to wealth, as you might expect."],[640.08,"Like we're not in a barter economy as subsistence farmers."],[644.66,"So our wealth doesn't take the form of how big our herds and flocks are, our wealth takes the form of money, of cash."],[654.26,"But you may notice, that some people at least do not view giving to the church as giving to God."],[665.35,"Why do I say that?"],[667.43,"Well, because once they have given the money to the church, if they're going to give money to the church, they want knowledge and sometimes even control of what exactly it's going to be used for."],[684.11,"That means you're not giving it to God."],[687.52,"It's not just a question of strings attached."],[690.18,"If I come and give you something."],[692.28,"If I say I am giving you a car, I'm going to give you a brand new car."],[696.2,"And I say, you can only drive it on Tuesdays and Thursdays, because I'm driving it on Saturday, Sunday, Monday, Wednesday."],[701.96,"And I'm going to watch the GPS, and I don't want you going anywhere that I don't want you to go."],[707.16,"Have I given you a car?"],[709.24,"Not really. It is not your car"],[713.65,"It is still my car."],[716.94,"And we tend to do that with God."],[718.46,"It's like, well, God tells us, frankly, let's just be blunt"],[725.52,"God tells us we're supposed to give 10% of everything back to him."],[729.76,"We don't like hearing that, because most of us don't actually do that, but that's what he says."],[735.5,"And there's not a good way out of that."],[737.36,"Because if you look at the church fathers, they say things like, yeah, Christians don't tithe."],[741.52,"They don't give 10%."],[742.48,"They give everything."],[743.44,"And then you're like, oh, well, let's go back to the 10%."],[748.23,"That's what he says."],[749.27,"And and the Bible is very blunt about this."],[752.63,"Eventually, in the Old Testament, we'll go get to Malachi, where God just straight out says, You people are all robbing me."],[757.91,"robb And the people say, How are weing you?"],[758.23,"ing me. And he says, You're not giv 10%"],[766.27,"Every bit of that that you keep, you are stealing from me."],[771.07,"So there's not a good way around that."],[772.91,"We just have to accept."],[775.12,"Since most of us aren't doing that."],[777.04,"We just have to accept that God has a standard, we're not living up to it."],[780.96,"And we can sort of try to do better."],[785.58,"But you don't reduce the you don't try and lower the standard so that I'm hitting it."],[789.76,"We just say, I know what God's standards is."],[793.04,"I know I should be doing more."],[794.8,"I really need to try to do more."],[796.9,"So this isn't to condemn anybody, because I'd be condemning myself, frankly, too."],[801.66,"But maybe because that's not been impressed on us, maybe because we know we're not meeting it, so we don't want to think about it."],[809.78,"We tend to act like, you know, oh, well, if I have a little extra money and I give it to the church, then I'm I'm doing a favor for this like organization that I'm a part of."],[824.34,"Or, you know, I'm gonna scrutinize."],[827.96,"What are they gonna use it for?"],[829.72,"What are they gonna they're gonna give the priest a raise?"],[832.92,"I don't like him."],[834.04,"Forget that. No."],[835.26,"Like, oh, they're putting a new roof on the building."],[837.58,"Well, we do need a new roof."],[838.7,"Okay, I'll give to that."],[840.03,"Um that again is skewed."],[843.77,"The idea is. we everything we have, God has given to us"],[850.85,"One of the ways he tells us to give thanks for that is to give him back a certain part of it."],[859.01,"10% being the going rate in the scripture."],[862.37,"And if we give it to him, then it's not ours anymore."],[869.17,"Okay. It's now God's money."],[873.09,"Okay. And God has appointed people in the church to handle his money."],[881.97,"And believe me, God will hold those people far more accountable for what they do with his money than you or I ever could."],[892.17,"We're big on this accountability in this world."],[894.82,"Like, no, no, no, no, no, no, no."],[896.92,"Like, trust me."],[898.04,"Someone who squanders God's money, someone who steals God's money, someone who embezzles God's money."],[904.49,"Is gonna answer to God for that."],[909.29,"I would much rather answer to a bunch of parishioners than have to answer to God."],[913.93,"I'd rather answer to a jury than answer to God about something like that."],[919.77,"Okay. So our responsibility is to give to God."],[926.25,"God can then do what he wants with it."],[928.25,"He's gonna do that through people he's appointed, and he's gonna hold them accountable for how they do it."],[935.09,"And us not trusting those people who got or not liking those people who got appointed, or whatever we think about them, and whatever we think about what they do, it's not our job to judge them."],[947.09,"They have a judge."],[954.61,"And who will hold them accountable for every penny and what they did with it."],[961.09,"But God will hold us accountable if we make excuses to not give."],[967.95,"If we use that as an excuse."],[970.85,"I don't want to be standing before Christ on the day of judgment and have him say, why did you spend so much of your money on yourself and give so little back to me?"],[979.17,"And I'm like, well, you know, if you if you look at the archdiocese audit, you can see that they they spent this money on this and this money on that."],[987.18,"So I didn't I didn't think they were good stewards."],[990.46,"But I expect Christ would say to me, So you kept it and spent it on yourself."],[998.03,"That dog don't hunt."],[1000.09,"That's not where you want to be."],[1002.51,"On the day of judgment."],[1004.83,"But so we see that principle here already."],[1007.63,"They're giving this to God."],[1009.47,"God is sharing some of that with the priests."],[1012.69,"So that the priests can have a livelihood so that the priests can serve as priests."],[1018.45,"And not have to worry about feeding their. families and these other things"],[1023.93,"So if a Levite comes from one of your cities, from where he dwells among all the children of Israel, as his soul desires, to the place the Lord chooses, then he may minister in the name of the Lord his God, as do all his brethren, the Levites who stand before the Lord."],[1042.33,"They shall have equal portions to eat, besides what comes from the sale of his paternal inheritance."],[1051.37,"So, what is that about?"],[1053.45,"How can he sell his paternal inheritance if he doesn't have a paternal inheritance?"],[1059.94,"And what was he doing with the paternal inheritance in one of your cities?"],[1065.9,"People from different tribes got married."],[1072.47,"So if his mother's a Levite and his father's a Judahite."],[1078.73,"This is Moses answering a question again."],[1082.43,"Because we've seen the first part of this before."],[1084.59,"We've seen before the Levite's inheritance is God, they don't have."],[1087.73,"They eat food from the sacrifices."],[1089.57,"All that we've seen before."],[1091.01,"But now Moses is asking a specific question."],[1094.21,"So a Judahite man marries a Levite woman."],[1099.09,"They have a kid."],[1100.93,"They have a son."],[1102.85,"Okay? Firstborn son, he inherits his dad's inheritance in Judah."],[1107.73,"But he's also, because of his mother, a Levite"],[1114.25,"And he says, you know what?"],[1117.85,"I want to live my life as a Levite."],[1123.14,"I want to follow in my uh grand maternal grandfather's footsteps."],[1128.9,"I want to be a Levite, I want to be a priest."],[1131.14,"And so he moves to where the sanctuary is from Judah."],[1136.26,"Moses is saying, if and when that kind of thing happens, then that paternal inheritance is sold."],[1144.1,"He's allowed to receive the money as a Levite, but now he's a Levite."],[1150.6,"And he lives the rest of his life as Levite."],[1152.48,"His children are Levites."],[1154.18,"He's no longer a Judite, he's a Levite."],[1158.42,"And then that land, if they had ever celebrated the year of Jubilee, that land could have been redeemed by another male relative, you know, 49 years in the future, who was living in Judah."],[1171.88,"Secondborn son, his son, grandson."],[1174.65,"Um, could redeem that land and bring it back into the family."],[1180.33,"So this is this is an example of what I meant about this being Moses' last time sort of exercising that authority he had."],[1189.46,"Which is to answer these questions of application."],[1192.74,"And when Moses answers that question, how do we handle this situation that isn't directly covered by what God directly said."],[1202.27,"What Moses said is what God says."],[1207.95,"Because that's the authority he's been given."],[1211.49,"To bind and to lose, to apply these things."],[1214.03,"And that's why it's encoded here in Deuteronomy."],[1216.11,"It's in here in Deuteronomy, just like the original commandment that came directly from God."],[1223.17,"It's not, there's not a distinction made."],[1225.33,"Oh, well, this is just Moses' opinion."],[1228.38,"This is what God said, but this is just Moses' opinion."],[1231.5,"It's all on a plane."],[1232.88,"That's the authority he was given."],[1235.92,"Now, if you enter the land of the Lord, you your God gives you shall not learn to do the abominations of those nations."],[1244.6,"So this is this would be the the uh opposite."],[1247.8,"Remember, they're being told to go in and wipe out those specific groups, those specific clans, those specific giant clans, because of these abominations they're committing."],[1258.6,"The goal is to wipe out the abominations, not the people."],[1263.1,"So any of the people who cease those abominations."],[1266.56,"If you're an Amalekite and you stop practicing these rituals of the Amalekites, you're not an Amalekite anymore."],[1273.54,"You can go and join another group."],[1276.58,"But so the opposite of them getting rid of these practices is them adopting these practices."],[1285.67,"And instead of putting a stop to it, they come in, they begin to practice them."],[1291.19,"They become like the people they're supposed to drive out."],[1293.83,"And now we're going to get some more particulars."],[1296.55,"Um, there shall not be found you among you anyone who purifies, who purifies his son or daughter in the fire, or one who practices divination, or a soothsayer, or one who interprets omens or a sorcerer, or one who conjures spells, or a medium, or a spiritist, or one who calls up the dead."],[1321.51,"Okay So the first one is being euphemistic."],[1326.15,"This is talking about uh sacrificing children to Molech"],[1331.63,"Not purifying children, it's sacrificing children by burning them alive."],[1337.47,"Which is something that was going on."],[1339.95,"So once again, these people who they're called to drive out and put an end to their abominations are not, you know, these pagans who love the land and are practicing a beautiful nature religion."],[1350.67,"Okay. They are burning babies alive, for one thing."],[1355.55,"To the demons they worship."],[1357.71,"This seems like a bad thing that we should put a stop to."],[1360.99,"Regardless of cultural sensitivities."],[1364.0,"But then we also get a list of other things."],[1366.32,"Uh soothsayers, that's involving that's oracles, like people being possessed by spirits and giving prophecies, sorcery, those who summon the spirits of the dead, etc. etc. do not do these things."],[1383.56,"For all who do these things are an abomination to the Lord your God, and because of these abominations, the Lord your God will destroy them before you."],[1392.28,"You shall be perfect before the Lord your God, for all these nations which you will dispossess, listen to soothsayers and diviners."],[1400.76,"But as for you, the Lord your God has not appointed such for you."],[1405.32,"You don't need to listen to demons talking through people."],[1409.48,"God is talking to you through Moses and then through Joshua, through the prophets."],[1415.32,"You don't need them to guide you"],[1416.32,"You don't need to talk to demons."],[1418.16,"You don't need to listen to them."],[1420.88,"Look where they guide you to."],[1423.12,"Somewhere around the time where they're killing their own children."],[1427.52,"You'd think they was, you know, maybe we shouldn't trust that guy."],[1432.74,"Maybe we shouldn't be listening to the spirits of the dead."],[1436.18,"And this is now directly tied to."],[1438.44,"Even though there's a break in the Orthodox Study Bible text here."],[1441.0,"There's not really a break in the text."],[1442.68,"The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from your brethren."],[1447.88,"Him you shall hear."],[1449.96,"According to all you asked from the Lord your God in Horeb in the day of the assembly, saying, Let us not hear again the voice of the Lord God, nor let us see his this great fire any more, lest we die."],[1465.68,"Then the Lord said to me, What they have spoken is good."],[1468.72,"I will raise up for them a prophet like you from among their brethren, and I will put my word in his mouth, and he shall speak to them all I command him."],[1478.72,"Therefore, whatever man will not listen to whatever the prophet speaks in my name, I will require it of him."],[1487.92,"So what is that's a weird expression."],[1491.58,"But the idea is this is what they're going to be judged by."],[1495.98,"This is this is the standard they're gonna be judged by, meaning what God's prophet says to them to do or not to. do"],[1504.58,"Like, as we were just saying, what Moses tells them to do or not to do is the same as God telling them it."],[1512.1,"So one day when they stand before God to be judged, what the prophet said to them is going to be part of."],[1521.92,"What they're judged on."],[1524.96,"They're judged on."],[1525.84,"Their obedience to the human authority who God put over them."],[1532.0,"We talked before way back when we were first talking about Moses' authority in Exodus."],[1537.42,"That this is where our understanding of the role of the bishop in the church comes from."],[1544.46,"By way of the apostles."],[1548.67,"God puts a human spiritual authority over us."],[1554.43,"And what they say, how they apply scriptures, as we come into today in the church with the bishop, the scriptures, the writings of the saints, the canons, all those things."],[1568.08,"That is the word of God to us."],[1578.24,"It's the opinion of the guy who God has put into the position of authority to give these opinions."],[1588.89,"So it is. binding on us"],[1595.17,"And our obedience or disobedience to it is part of our judgment."],[1599.97,"This is why, for example, St."],[1601.65,"Siloon says, if you're obedient to spiritual authority, you can remember that God only punishes sin once."],[1612.29,"Meaning, if you are obedient and you are misled, God is going to hold the person who misled you accountable."],[1623.79,"A bishop gives you permission to have a third marriage, and that was a really bad idea, that's not on you."],[1629.47,"That's on the bishop."],[1633.07,"From God's. on the bishop, I mean God is going to judge them"],[1639.43,"We've said this several times in this Bible study, but this is this is how that authority works."],[1646.07,"We all have to give an account to God for ourselves and for all those who are under our authority."],[1656.39,"So if you are a parent, you have to give an account for yourself and for your children."],[1664.35,"You are a godparent."],[1665.55,"You have to give an account for yourself and for your godchildren."],[1668.27,"That's a serious responsibility."],[1673.95,"You're a bit too hasty with uh some agree."],[1679.15,"No, but we we have to give an account."],[1681.23,"Not that we're hold accountable for everything they do, but we're held accountable for what we said and did in regard to them, how we guided them, the example we set for them."],[1692.59,"They choose not to follow."],[1694.53,"If we're giving them good advice, and telling them the way they should go."],[1698.52,"And they go off in the other direction, that's not on you."],[1702.88,"But our interactions with them."],[1705.9,"I, as a priest, have to give an account to God on the day of judgment for all of you."],[1713.71,"Bishop has to give an account for all of you and me and all the other clergy."],[1720.11,"Everyone else he had authority over."],[1721.15,"This is St"],[1724.55,"That's why these things are seeing."],[1728.31,"Paul's saying, not many should presume to be teachers."],[1731.59,"We all want to be teachers, we all want to be the boss, we all want to be in charge, because we're not thinking about that accountability."],[1739.19,"Think about the level of accountability the emperor had."],[1763.83,"It's a hierarchical system."],[1765.75,"Not just the church, reality"],[1768.83,"There's people above us who we're accountable to, and there are people below us who we're accountable for."],[1777.15,"But it's all accountability all the way up and all the way down."],[1781.87,"It's all responsibility all the way up and all the way down."],[1785.31,"At no point is authority like, aha, I have power over other people."],[1792.83,"No, you have a duty."],[1795.31,"You have responsibility."],[1796.43,"And the higher you are in that hierarchy, the more duty and the more responsibility you have."],[1802.83,"That's why we pray for all the people above us."],[1807.57,"Because we know from whatever level of responsibility we have."],[1811.47,"We can then imagine the people above us who are higher up, kind of the yoke that's on them, on their shoulders."],[1821.23,"And how much they need our prayers."],[1823.79,"So yeah, that's the responsibility angle."],[1827.79,"But we are responsible to the people who God has put above us."],[1835.08,"To follow their direction and instruction within their sphere of authority."],[1844.54,"That doesn't mean you slavishly be like, you know, calling your godfather, being like, what cereal should I eat?"],[1852.34,"I I'm worried this one has too much sugar, but the bran is too much fiber, and I don't know."],[1859.96,"No. Like, that's not right."],[1863.02,"But there are areas of life in which they are our guide."],[1868.64,"And when they speak to us about those things, then we need to listen."],[1875.01,"And we need to be obedient."],[1880.69,"Because in those places, obeying them is obeying God."],[1886.31,"And this is so thorough going in the New Testament that St."],[1890.79,"Paul is going to say, even though it's very clear from everything St."],[1893.99,"Paul says, that slavery as an institution was unjust."],[1899.07,"What does he say to people who are to enslaved people in the churches?"],[1906.67,"He says, obey your quote unquote master as the Lord."],[1914.11,"Because you're really serving Christ."],[1916.91,"Not that human who claims to own you."],[1920.67,"But whatever prophet speaks impiously in my name, a word I have not ordered him to speak, or who speaks in the name of different gods, that prophet shall die."],[1931.23,"We really should have cleaned house with the Pentecostals after uh the 2020 election."],[1937.07,"Yeah. So. So, this is not, they have have. to a better than 50% average"],[1945.88,"Okay, this is one time they come and say, the Lord says, or the Lord told me, and it's not true, stoned to death."],[1955.64,"Yes, just say I think."],[1957.56,"Just say in my opinion."],[1959.24,"That's how they get around it, Jules."],[1961.24,"Well, no, they don't, though."],[1962.92,"That's the problem."],[1963.8,"They don't. They keep saying God said this, God revealed this to me, God, the Holy Spirit says that's blasphemy."],[1972.14,"And it's not just they, I've heard Orthodox people do this."],[1975.08,"That's blasphemy. You are taking your own ideas, sometimes your own stupid ideas, and attributing them to God."],[1981.64,"That's blasphemy. You see, St."],[1985.73,"Paul do this."],[1986.45,"St. Paul says this in the text of scriptures, I don't have a word from the Lord on this."],[1992.61,"But in my opinion, it's not that hard to do."],[1998.19,"To say that."],[2000.05,"To say, I don't think God has given a clear direction on this particular issue."],[2005.57,"But here's how it seems to me."],[2008.53,"And here's why I think that."],[2010.93,"And I could be wrong."],[2014.75,"Yeah, because this is one time."],[2017.79,"One time. And I have to, I have to pick on our charismatic and Pentecostal friends a little bit here."],[2024.48,"Because when you confront one of one of them with this, and I've done this a few times, you get the most inane arguments I've ever heard in my life."],[2035.96,"Which is, well, that was the Old Testament."],[2039.4,"Prophecy in the New Testament isn't like that."],[2042.12,"It's not 100%."],[2044.28,"So in every other way, the New Testament is the fulfillment of the Old Testament."],[2050.92,"It is filled full."],[2052.2,"It is better."],[2053.0,"It is superior."],[2054.2,"Except prophecy. Prophecy stinks now."],[2058.04,"That's why I say it's one of the most inane arguments I've ever heard in my life."],[2061.89,"Like it makes no sense."],[2062.93,"It's like, no, you are calling things prophecies that aren't prophecies."],[2067.49,"You are calling vibes your gut."],[2072.91,"What passes for your common sense, you're calling that prophecy."],[2077.79,"That's not what prophecy ever was."],[2082.35,"Old or New Testament."],[2084.73,"What makes it where we get to Jeremiah?"],[2086.65,"We'll see, one of the things that makes someone a prophet is that they have stood before God, like in person."],[2094.97,"If you haven't done that, you're not a prophet and you're not prophesying."],[2102.49,"Nothing you say is prophet if you haven't done that, according to Jeremiah."],[2108.09,"The apostles all stood before God directly, including St."],[2111.53,"Paul. Christ appeared to him multiple times."],[2115.86,"Not me. I'm not a prophet, nor the son of a prophet."],[2120.71,"Nothing I say is prophecy in the strict sense."],[2126.79,"So yeah, that is that is this weird watered down thing."],[2135.11,"Magic eight ball guesswork is prophecy now in the new covenant."],[2139.59,"Used to be way better in the good old days before Christ."],[2145.35,"The whole dog don't hunt"],[2148.67,"Do you still have prophets in the Orthodox churches?"],[2151.55,"I know there was like all the prophecy that were kind of blowing up over like with other rand stuff and all that."],[2159.31,"Oh, yeah, yeah."],[2163.39,"Well, no, I mean there's prophets in the New Testament."],[2165.31,"We know, I mean, Agabas in the book of Acts, for example."],[2169.83,"But Agabas comes and tells Paul, when you go to Jerusalem, you're gonna be arrested, and you're gonna be there, and then that happens."],[2177.91,"It's a hundred percent still with Agabus."],[2180.71,"He also says there's gonna be a famine, and then there's a famine in the book of Acts."],[2184.76,"So there are still people, but we talk about it in different ways now in the church."],[2191.69,"So the saints who we talk about having had the vision of Christ in uncreated glory, that experience is the same experience the prophets had when they stood before God."],[2201.77,"They're seeing Christ"],[2203.57,"Like Isaiah or Ezekiel when they see God."],[2208.73,"Yeah. So an example of a later prophet, Saint Simeon the New Theologian would be a latter day prophet."],[2219.69,"Don't get excited, Mormons."],[2224.46,"Like St. Simeon the New Theologian, say Seraphim of Serev."],[2228.68,"So there are people who still have that experience and and who who right have certain gifts."],[2237.74,"So there was a uh where I went to seminary, there was a monastic around."],[2242.3,"around. Who would come sometimes who was kind of scary, especially to me"],[2248.74,"I've talked before, I know in this Bible study about how I'm terrified by holy people."],[2253.3,"Primarily because I figured they'll know I'm a fake."],[2278.74,"Out of the blue randomly, he called his mom, and his mom had just gotten a cancer diagnosis."],[2286.34,"So there are still people with the kind of prophetic gifts that we see in scripture."],[2296.14,"They don't uh raise money on television or the internet."],[2303.18,"They don't sell you water that they claim is from the Jordan River."],[2306.46,"Uh they don't they don't smack people in the head at Crusades."],[2311.74,"Yeah. They're rail thin and that's they they don't do any of that."],[2317.0,"But yeah, they they don't sell you food slot buckets for the coming apocalypse."],[2323.18,"That's not profit."],[2324.22,"But there there are but but that that's also we wouldn't we wouldn't say like any wonder working saint or no, but if they told me to do something, I'd do it."],[2337.3,"Yeah. Yeah. Yeah."],[2342.69,"Yeah. If St."],[2344.05,"Silwan had told me directly to do something, I would do it."],[2346.95,"Like I didn't know if there were like I don't I didn't know if there was like a very clear like harsh distinction of a theologian versus uh Yeah, I didn't wonder, so I that's why I was asking."],[2358.55,"No, no. But it's just there there are people with who have had those experiences and have those kind of gifts."],[2363.91,"So we would but we would say that."],[2366.55,"And who speak things out of that experience that then are to be taken very seriously."],[2371.27,"So all of those people would have experienced crises."],[2375.99,"We've had these kind of experience, yes."],[2377.35,"So yeah Yeah."],[2378.43,"Yeah. And they're few and far between, and they don't come and make demands on you."],[2383.65,"Like they're not going to show up at your door and be like, I'm moving in with you for the next year, and I want you to feed and clothe me and this kind of thing."],[2390.67,"Um. I mean, you laugh, but I no, I've known people like I I knew I knew a woman who is uh Filipino, and that happened with her family in the Philippines."],[2402.27,"Somebody showed up and claimed they were a prophet from God and demanded to live with them, and her family like put this person up in their house and like fed them and gave them money and stuff."],[2415.19,"Because right, like that still happens."],[2417.55,"Like places. Yeah."],[2420.35,"So, yeah. But the people who uh are for real, that they aren't doing things like that"],[2426.95,"Now, if you should say in your heart, how shall we know the word the Lord has not spoken?"],[2431.91,"Whatever word a prophet speaks in the name of the Lord, if the thing does not happen or come to pass, that is the thing the Lord has not spoken, the prophet spoke that word impiously, you shall stay away from it."],[2445.75,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2453.11,"Father Stephen's email address is whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2458.39,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":22.8,"lv":2,"h":"Catch-up: middle of Deuteronomy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Back after <b>Lent and Pascha break</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>34 chapters</b>; finished 17 → \"smack in the middle\" of the book</li><li class=\"d0\">Most of Deuteronomy = Moses' <b>final oration</b>, last sermon</li><li class=\"d1\">preparing to pass leadership to <b>Joshua</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people on <b>plains of Moab</b>, about to cross Jordan into Canaan</li><li class=\"d0\">Last topic: <b>feasts</b> once in the land</li><li class=\"d1\">Deuteronomy = <b>second law</b>; reminding of things in Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses highlighting and <b>reapplying</b> to new setting</li></ul>"},{"t":185.26,"lv":3,"h":"From camp to land","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>42 years</b> in desert camp; <b>second generation</b>, first generation dead</li><li class=\"d0\">Life known: <b>tabernacle in the middle</b>, tribes camped around</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Day of Atonement</b> built on that camp life</li><li class=\"d0\">Now <b>settled</b>, spread across land; sanctuary in one place</li><li class=\"d1\">travel to sanctuary → Atonement, <b>Passover</b> a little different for those far away</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses reapplying feast commandments to <b>new context</b></li></ul>"},{"t":286.36,"lv":3,"h":"Civil government and Moses' last authority","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Same for other things; most recently <b>kings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">return at <b>1 Samuel</b>: \"every Puritan's favorite misinterpreted passage\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Civil government</b> not needed in a desert camp</li><li class=\"d1\">towns, cities, villages → functions to organize, people in charge</li><li class=\"d1\">camp-era <b>elders</b> adapted to new situation</li><li class=\"d0\">More than a <b>farewell address</b> (Eisenhower's - \"warned us about everything since 1960\")</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Last time</b> Moses uses God-given authority: apply what God spoke to people's lives</li><li class=\"d1\">why this is the <b>last book of Moses</b></li><li class=\"d1\">handing authority to <b>Joshua</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Changing topics here</li></ul>"},{"t":431.37,"lv":2,"h":"18:1-5 - Levites have no inheritance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Priests, Levites, all tribe of Levi: <b>no part nor inheritance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">burnt offerings = their portion; \"the <b>Lord is their inheritance</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Inheritance = <b>land allotments</b> (Numbers) - each tribe, clan, family</li><li class=\"d1\">not that they can't pass things to children</li><li class=\"d0\">Most of Israel = <b>subsistence farming</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Levites have families, no land → how do they eat?</li><li class=\"d0\">Not a punishment</li><li class=\"d1\">called to serve God <b>full time</b>: sanctuary, spiritual needs, sacrifices</li><li class=\"d1\">can't also operate a farm - \"they can't do both\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>18:3-5</b>: priests get <b>shoulder, cheeks, stomach</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>first fruits</b> of grain, wine, oil, fleece</li><li class=\"d1\">chosen \"to stand before the Lord... minister and bless in his name\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Tithes and offerings: portion to priests</li></ul>"},{"t":594.1,"lv":3,"h":"Giving to God, not to the church","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Logic: people bring it to <b>God</b>; if God gives part to Levites, no protest</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern wealth = <b>cash</b>, not herds</li><li class=\"d0\">Some don't see giving to church as <b>giving to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">want knowledge, even <b>control</b>, of its use → \"you're not giving it to God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Car analogy: \"drive it only Tuesdays and Thursdays\", watching GPS</li><li class=\"d1\">\"have I given you a car? Not really\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God says give <b>10%</b></li><li class=\"d1\">church fathers: Christians don't tithe, they give <b>everything</b> - then \"back to the 10%\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Malachi</b>: \"you are robbing me\" - the 10% you keep = stealing</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't <b>lower the standard</b> - know it, try to do more</li><li class=\"d1\">not condemning; \"I'd be condemning myself\"</li></ul>"},{"t":801.66,"lv":3,"h":"It is God's money now","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We act like giving is <b>a favor to an organization</b></li><li class=\"d1\">scrutinize: \"give the priest a raise? I don't like him\" / \"new roof - okay\" → <b>skewed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Everything we have <b>God gave</b>; giving back part = thanks, 10% the \"going rate\"</li><li class=\"d1\">once given, <b>not ours</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God appointed people in the church to handle his money</li><li class=\"d1\">he holds them <b>far more accountable</b> than we could</li><li class=\"d1\">\"rather answer to a jury than to God\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not our job to <b>judge</b> them - \"they have a judge\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God holds <b>us</b> accountable if we use that as an excuse</li><li class=\"d1\">\"archdiocese audit\" excuse → \"you kept it and spent it on yourself\" - <b>\"that dog don't hunt\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Principle here: God shares with priests for <b>livelihood</b>, to serve without worrying about family</li></ul>"},{"t":1023.93,"lv":2,"h":"18:6-8 - The Levite who moves to the sanctuary","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Levite comes from a city to the chosen place → ministers, <b>equal portions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"besides what comes from the <b>sale of his paternal inheritance</b>\" - what is that?</li><li class=\"d0\">Tribes intermarried: <b>Judahite</b> father, <b>Levite</b> mother</li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn inherits father's land in <b>Judah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wants to live as a Levite, follow his <b>maternal grandfather</b>; moves to sanctuary</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: land is <b>sold</b>, he receives the money</li><li class=\"d1\">now a Levite for life; <b>children Levites</b>, no longer Judahite</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jubilee</b>: male relative in Judah could redeem it 49 years on</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses <b>answering a question</b> again - last use of his authority</li></ul>"},{"t":1180.33,"lv":3,"h":"Moses' word = God's word","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Application questions not directly covered: \"what Moses said is what God says\"</li><li class=\"d1\">authority to <b>bind and loose</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Encoded in Deuteronomy just like the original commandment</li><li class=\"d1\">no distinction \"this is just Moses' opinion\"; <b>all on a plane</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1235.92,"lv":2,"h":"18:9-14 - Abominations of the nations","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Don't learn the <b>abominations</b> of those nations</li><li class=\"d1\">go in to wipe out specific clans, giant clans, for abominations</li><li class=\"d1\">goal = wipe out the <b>abominations, not the people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Amalekite who stops the rituals \"isn't an Amalekite anymore\", can join another group</li><li class=\"d0\">Opposite = <b>adopting</b> the practices, becoming like those driven out</li><li class=\"d0\">List: <b>purifies son or daughter in fire</b>, divination, soothsayer, omens, sorcerer, spells, medium, spiritist, <b>calls up the dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">first is a <b>euphemism</b>: sacrificing children to <b>Molech</b>, burning alive</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"pagans who love the land and practice a beautiful nature religion\" - burning babies to demons</li><li class=\"d1\">soothsayers = oracles, people <b>possessed by spirits</b> giving prophecies</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Perfect</b> before the Lord; those nations listen to soothsayers</li><li class=\"d1\">you don't need <b>demons talking through people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God speaks through Moses, Joshua, <b>the prophets</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"look where they guide you\" - killing their own children</li></ul>"},{"t":1436.18,"lv":2,"h":"18:15-19 - A prophet like Moses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Tied directly to previous, despite break in Orthodox Study Bible</li><li class=\"d0\">Lord will raise up a <b>prophet like me</b> - \"him you shall hear\"</li><li class=\"d1\">per request at <b>Horeb</b>: \"let us not hear again the voice... lest we die\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what they have spoken is good\"; God puts <b>his word in his mouth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Whoever won't listen: \"I will <b>require it of him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">standard of judgment = what God's prophet says to do or not do</li><li class=\"d1\">obedience to <b>human authority</b> God put over them</li><li class=\"d0\">Source of the <b>bishop</b>'s role, by way of the apostles (Exodus on Moses' authority)</li><li class=\"d1\">bishop, scriptures, writings of the saints, canons = <b>word of God to us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">binding; obedience part of our judgment</li></ul>"},{"t":1595.17,"lv":3,"h":"Accountability: God punishes sin once","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Silouan</b>: obedient to spiritual authority, God punishes sin <b>only once</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if obedient and misled, God holds <b>the one who misled you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bishop permits a <b>third marriage</b> - \"that's on the bishop\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Everyone accounts for self and those under authority</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>parent</b>: self and children; <b>godparent</b>: godchildren</li><li class=\"d1\">accountable for what we <b>said and did</b>, guidance, example - not their choices</li><li class=\"d1\">priest answers for all of you; bishop for all clergy and everyone</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul</b>: \"not many should presume to be teachers\" - we want to be the boss, not thinking of accountability</li><li class=\"d1\">think of the <b>emperor</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1763.83,"lv":2,"h":"Hierarchy as duty","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Hierarchical system - \"not just the church, <b>reality</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">people above we're accountable to, below we're accountable for</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>responsibility all the way up and all the way down</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Authority is never \"I have power over others\" → <b>\"you have a duty\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">higher up, more duty</li><li class=\"d0\">Why we <b>pray for those above us</b> - the yoke on their shoulders</li><li class=\"d0\">We're responsible to those over us: follow <b>direction within their sphere</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not slavishly - \"calling your godfather: what cereal should I eat?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">in their areas, <b>obeying them is obeying God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">NT thorough: Paul on <b>slavery</b> (clearly unjust) says \"obey your master as the Lord\"</li><li class=\"d1\">really serving <b>Christ</b>, not the human who claims to own you</li></ul>"},{"t":1920.67,"lv":2,"h":"18:20 - The false prophet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Prophet speaks <b>impiously in my name</b>, or in name of other gods → <b>dies</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Aside: \"should have cleaned house with the Pentecostals after the 2020 election\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The Lord says\" / \"the Lord told me\" and it's untrue → <b>stoned</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"just say in my opinion\" - they don't; \"God revealed this to me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Orthodox people do it too → <b>blasphemy</b>: your own ideas attributed to God</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul</b>: \"I don't have a word from the Lord on this, but in my opinion\"</li><li class=\"d1\">say \"I don't think God has given clear direction... here's how it seems to me... I could be wrong\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2017.79,"lv":2,"h":"Charismatic arguments","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Their reply: \"that was the Old Testament; NT prophecy isn't 100%\"</li><li class=\"d1\">NT fulfills OT in every way - <b>\"except prophecy. Prophecy stinks now\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"most inane argument\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Calling <b>vibes, gut, common sense</b> prophecy - not what it ever was, either Testament</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jeremiah</b>: a prophet has <b>stood before God</b>, in person</li><li class=\"d1\">apostles all did, incl. Paul (Christ appeared multiple times)</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm not a prophet, nor the son of a prophet\"; nothing he says is prophecy in the strict sense</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Magic eight ball guesswork is prophecy now\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2148.67,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: Prophets in the Orthodox Church?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: still prophets in the Orthodox church?</li><li class=\"d1\">yes: NT prophets, <b>Agabus</b> in Acts</li><li class=\"d1\">told Paul he'd be arrested in Jerusalem; predicted a <b>famine</b> - 100%</li><li class=\"d0\">Spoken of differently now</li><li class=\"d1\">saints with <b>vision of Christ in uncreated glory</b> = same experience as prophets before God</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Isaiah, Ezekiel</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>St. Symeon the New Theologian</b> - \"don't get excited, Mormons\"; <b>Seraphim of Sarov</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2237.74,"lv":3,"h":"Holy people and false prophets","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Seminary monastic, \"kind of scary\" - he's terrified by holy people, figures \"they'll know I'm a fake\"</li><li class=\"d1\">out of the blue called his mom, who had just got a <b>cancer diagnosis</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Real ones don't <b>raise money on TV</b>, sell Jordan water, smack people at crusades, sell <b>food buckets</b> for the apocalypse</li><li class=\"d1\">\"rail thin\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Few and far between; don't make demands</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I'm moving in for a year, feed and clothe me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Filipino woman's family put up a self-proclaimed <b>prophet</b>, fed him, gave money</li><li class=\"d0\">If St. Silouan told him directly to do something, he'd do it</li><li class=\"d0\">Real ones' words out of that experience \"taken very seriously\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2426.95,"lv":2,"h":"18:21-22 - Test of a prophet","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"How shall we know the word the Lord has not spoken?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Prophet speaks in Lord's name, <b>thing does not come to pass</b> → <b>Lord has not spoken</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spoke impiously; \"you shall <b>stay away from it</b>\"</li></ul>"}]});
